# User manual (`doc/manual/`)

Pilots read the LaTeX user manual, not `doc/*.rst`. Those `.rst` files are
contributor docs.

## When to update

If a change is **user-visible** (new or changed UI, setting, InfoBox, menu,
gesture, file format a pilot uses, installation step), update the **English**
manual in `doc/manual/en/` and add a `NEWS.txt` bullet.

Do **not** update the manual for pure refactors, CI, or developer-only APIs.

## Where to edit

Edit English first (`doc/manual/en/`). Do not require `de/`, `fr/`, or
`pt_BR/` in the same change unless you are doing a translation pass.

| Topic | Chapter |
|-------|--------|
| UI, menus, gestures | `ch02_user_interface.tex` |
| Navigation, map, Goto | `ch03_navigation.tex` |
| Tasks | `ch04_xc_tasks.tex` |
| MacCready, polar, final glide | `ch05_glide_computer.tex` |
| Atmosphere, thermal, wind | `ch06_atmosphere_and_instruments.tex` |
| Airspace, FLARM, traffic | `ch07_airspace_and_flarm.tex` |
| Devices, radios, logger | `ch08_avionics_and_airframe.tex` |
| InfoBoxes | `ch10_infobox_reference.tex` |
| Configuration / Setup | `ch11_configuration.tex` |
| Waypoints, airspace files, maps | `ch12_data_files.tex` |
| Install / platforms | `installation.tex` |
| Third-party devices | `integration.tex` |

Master file: `doc/manual/en/XCSoar-manual.tex`. Build with `make manual`.

## NEWS.txt

Manual updates that pilots would notice also get a `* documentation` bullet.
See `.cursor/rules/news.txt.mdc`.
